A||||5||daved||Towing an '84 Auto on a dolly||||1||
Z||000000||daved||03-24-2001||10:03 PM||||Anyone know why U-haul states in their towing booklet <BR>"Always load vehicle-in-tow facing forward. NEVER back onto the tow dolly"...and..."Towing a rearward-facing vehicle will result in an uncontrollable, dangerous combination"<BR>If the steering is locked straight ahead, then how can it make any difference?<BR>I assume since it's an auto, I can't tow it front first without pulling the drive axles.<BR>How do you guys tow an auto tranny Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||03-24-2001||10:35 PM||||i heard about the same thing but i was already there to get the car, 150 mls from home. i put it in neutral and brought it home. didn't seem to affect it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||03-24-2001||11:08 PM||||Mine came via dolly and was loaded backwards...no problems encountered.<BR>Gary||||reg||14
Z||000003||mrfiero||03-24-2001||11:18 PM||||They say don't tow a car backwards because the majority of cars out there have the engines in the front.  That would place the majority of the weight to the rear causing the towed car to possibly fishtail, etc.<P>Since the Fieros motor is out back that problem doesn't apply to us......just the opposite, actually.  If you towed a Fiero facing forward there would be too much weight out back (off the dolly) causing potential problems on a long trip.<P>I, and MANY others, have successfully towed Fieros cross country on a dolly facing backwards.  The only thing I would do is cover the exhaust tips with  something to keep rain out......otherwise they act as funnels!   I found that out the hard way.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||03-24-2001||11:29 PM||||Thanks guys for the quick replies.  <BR>MrFiero, your logic makes a lot of sense, and I will proceed with the dolly.  Dont believe all you see in print applies here. Found a '84 in Toronto with T-tops.  Scruffy, but looks restorable...cheap too, if I can get it home, thanks, Dave||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||03-25-2001||06:18 AM||||Tow it backwards. I have towed them both ways. Forward because because of front end damage and backward which puts most of the weight on the dolly axle and allows you to use e-brake and park to help stabalize the car on the dolly. Rear facing towed noticeable brtter. Just make sure your hood and trunk are latched.||||reg||1
